* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* Example Pin Definition File for QSymGen3
*
* Implements: Microchip PIC16F15213/PIC16F15214 devices
* Author:     Robert Dunn
* Revised:    2026.06.26
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
*
* D = Description for symbol
*
D Microchip PIC16F15213/PIC16F15214
*
*
* P = Part names for (1) selection in symbol properties and (2) software
* simulator initialization.  Note that the part numbers must match
* in case as used in MDBCore.  (ATtiny85 works; ATTINY85 does not.)
* 
P PIC16F15213 PIC16F15214
*
*
* R = DLL output pin internal resistance (ROUT) for generated Device Schematic
* Default is 1. Shown explicitly here for tutorial purposes.
R 1
*
*
* Pin Definitions
*   V = Supply voltage name (required; must match simulator name)
*   G = Ground pin (required; not used in simulator but relevant to QSpice)
*   I = Input-only pin
*   O = Output-only pin
*   B = Bi-directional (GPIO) pin
*   K = Simulation clock input (required)
*   X = Spacer for pretty symbols
*
V VDD
B RA0 ICSPDAT 
B RA1 ICSPCLK
B RA2 
X
I RA3 MCLR/VPP
B RA4 
B RA5 
G VSS
K SIMCLK [Not A Device Pin]
*
*** EOF ***